Chapter 10: Sliding Window + Hashing

This is where medium problems begin.

Example:

Longest substring without repeating characters.

Need to know

Have I already seen this character?

Brain says

Hashing

Need a moving window

Sliding Window

So the solution is

Sliding Window

+

Hashing

Many famous interview questions use this combination.

Complexity

Without Sliding Window

O(n × k)

With Sliding Window

O(n)

Each element enters the window once and leaves at most once.
